id: pm-slack-standup-lvgk
title: "Refuse a line break in a cmd.exe launch argument, which quoting cannot contain"
description: "quoteWindowsArg only quotes an argument containing one of tab, space, double quote, ampersand, pipe, angle bracket, parenthesis or caret, and the existing refusal covers only percent-delimited names. A carriage return or line feed is in neither set, so it reached the cmd tail unquoted, and cmd ends the command at a line break and reads the remainder as a separate command."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-09-05T18:03:51.515Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-05T18:14:40.488Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-05T18:14:40.447Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-05T18:14:40.447Z"
claim_principal: claude-orchestrator
author: claude-orchestrator
resolution: "Refused carriage return and line feed in a cmd.exe launch argument, since quoting cannot contain a command boundary."
expected_result: "An argument containing a line break is refused before reaching the cmd tail, and the refusal names what was refused."
actual_result: "Both carriage return and line feed throw CommandError naming the line break; release:check exits 0 and the guard test fails 1 of 38 when the guard is removed."
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-05T18:14:39.761Z",claude-orchestrator,"CodeQL alert js/shell-command-constructed-from-input at index.ts:1149 pointed at the cmd.exe launch tail. The existing hardening is sound for metacharacters: quoteWindowsArg implements the CommandLineToArgvW backslash and quote rules in a single linear pass, and assertNoCmdVariableExpansion fails closed on a percent-delimited name because cmd expands it even inside quotes. Reading those two guards against each other exposed a gap neither covers. quoteWindowsArg only quotes when the argument matches its special-character class, which is tab, space, double quote, ampersand, pipe, angle brackets, parentheses and caret. A carriage return or line feed is not in that class, so an argument whose only special character is a line break was emitted into the tail unquoted. Quoting would not have helped in any case: a line break is a command boundary for cmd rather than a metacharacter, so cmd ends the command there and reads the remainder as a fresh command on the same /c tail. The argument is therefore refused, matching how the percent case is handled. Both carriage return and line feed are covered because a lone carriage return still ends the line. Verified non-vacuous by deleting the guard and re-running the suite: the new test fails 1 of 38, and passes 38 of 38 with the guard restored."
files[2]{path,scope}:
  index.ts,project
  test/fetch-all-items.test.ts,project
tests[1]{command,scope,provenance{author,created_at,source_kind,source_ref}}:
